  "answer": "Based on Table 2.2 in the ICILS 2023 International Report (ISCED 1 / primary education), I counted the \"◇ Available but not compulsory to teach\" entries across all 8 categories (4 for CIL + 4 for CT) for each country.\n\n**Countries with the most \"Available but not compulsory\" categories at ISCED 1:**\n\n| Country | CIL (◇) | CT (◇) | Total |\n|---------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **Netherlands** | 4 | 4 | **8** |\n| **United States** | 4 | 4 | **8** |\n| Oman | 3 | 4 | 7 |\n| Spain | 2 | 4 | 6 |\n| Austria | 2 | 3 | 5 |\n| Uruguay | 4 | 1 | 5 |\n| Serbia | 2 | 3 | 5 |\n\n**Netherlands and United States are tied for the most** — both had all 8 categories (every CIL and CT category at ISCED 1) marked as \"Available but not compulsory to teach.\"",
